## Local modifications

- Mapped skills record a verified `upstream.commit` and `baseline: "verified"`.
  The `contentHash` is the upstream pre-stamp content identity; `snapshotHash` describes the
  vendored bytes after provenance stamping.
- Any future frontmatter source/version stamps added by this registry are local
  modifications to the upstream files, not upstream-provided metadata.
- Bootstrap `firstSeen` timestamps are derived from the current git commit author
  timestamp because no deterministic per-path upstream history exists yet.

